import OpcodeFilters from '../../../../components/OpcodeFilters.astro';

This page documents the current state of the AVM and may include AVM versions that have not yet been approved and adopted by all node operators.

The **Size** field lists an opcode's total encoded length in bytes: the opcode bytes plus its immediate arguments. It is omitted when an immediate has variable length. Constant opcodes such as `pushint`, `pushbytes` and `intcblock` carry their values inline; `b`, `bz`, `bnz` and `callsub` encode their relative target offset as a `varint (zigzag)` (see the notes under `bnz`); and `switch` and `match` take a variable-length list of `int16` targets. Opcodes that take an immediate also carry an **Immediate Parameters** note describing what each argument expects. In a **Field Reference** table, **Index** is the field's number: the value of the field immediate in the bytecode. Each table lists only the fields that opcode's immediate can name, so the numbers can skip.

